    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 11 with a lineup heavily reliant on top-of-the-order speed to combat our league\u2019s scarcity in stolen bases. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) is our undisputed strongest play today. With an assumed lead-off role against a vulnerable arm in Ryan Feltner (xERA 4.55), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% park boost and significant platoon advantages, making him the only player in our squad to breach the 80-point threshold. We are also closely tracking **Chase Meidroth** (58.15) and **Carson Benge** (56.54); both are locked into lead-off spots, providing the efficiency required to generate runs while maximizing stolen base opportunities against favorable pitching matchups.\n\nWhile our core remains focused on high-efficiency starters, the marginal decisions highlight the importance of plate discipline and matchup leverage. **Colt Keith** (57.27) marginally edges out **Lars Nootbaar** (53.91) for a starting spot today, largely due to a favorable platoon matchup and the potential for a \"slow delivery\" bonus against the opposing starter, which we project will provide a boost to his stolen base equity. **Luke Raley** (54.59) remains a high-floor start despite a pending lineup status, as his power profile is buoyed by a significant 16% park factor adjustment. **Dillon Dingler** (43.28) rounds out the catcher slot; while his matchup against a sub-4.00 xERA arm like Matthews presents risk, his solid xwOBA of 0.386 keeps him above our bench threshold. We are currently navigating a quiet day for our high-impact bench pieces, as **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** are all sidelined by team off-days, forcing us to rely on our active roster depth to maintain our category leads.",
